<!DOCTYPE html>

<html lang="en">

<head>
    <title>Learn - RaagVerse</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>

<body>

<%- include("partials/navbar") %>

<main>

    <section>
        <h1>Learn</h1>
        <p>Indian Classical Music — A Simple Guide</p>
    </section>


    <section>

        <div>
            <h2>Aaroh</h2>
            <p>
                The ascending movement of notes in a raag.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Avroh</h2>
            <p>
                The descending movement of notes in a raag.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Rasa</h2>
            <p>
                The emotional character or feeling expressed through a raag.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Samay</h2>
            <p>
                The traditional time of day associated with a raag.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Samvaadi</h2>
            <p>
                The second most important note of a raag, which complements the Vaadi.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Swar</h2>
            <p>
                The musical notes used in Indian classical music.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Taal</h2>
            <p>
                A rhythmic cycle used to organize rhythm in Indian classical music.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Thaat</h2>
            <p>
                A system of classifying raags based on a group of seven musical notes.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>Vaadi</h2>
            <p>
                The most prominent or important note of a raag.
            </p>
        </div>

    </section>

</main>

<%- include("partials/footer") %>

</body>

</html>
